WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.416
Meet DeskCharm.

2
00:00:01.466 --> 00:00:09.727
It is a little charm that hangs from the top
of your screen, sways as your mouse passes by,
and keeps you company while you work.

3
00:00:09.777 --> 00:00:13.850
And now and then, a friendly visitor strolls
along your taskbar.

4
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.084
Getting started is easy.

5
00:00:17.134 --> 00:00:24.029
Run the installer — no admin rights needed —
and DeskCharm starts right away, in the
top-right corner.

6
00:00:24.079 --> 00:00:29.000
Its tray icon, near the clock, opens Settings,
hides the charm, or quits.

7
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:32.527
The charm is made for touching.

8
00:00:32.577 --> 00:00:35.821
Grab it and fling it, and it swings on a real
string.

9
00:00:35.871 --> 00:00:40.483
Rest your cursor on it, and it glows softly,
breathing in and out with you.

10
00:00:40.533 --> 00:00:42.223
Double-click to ring a bell.

11
00:00:42.273 --> 00:00:42.844
Rough day?

12
00:00:42.894 --> 00:00:46.325
Click it quickly, again and again, and smash
it to calm.

13
00:00:47.975 --> 00:00:53.493
Right-click for the quick menu: breathing,
focus, your tasks, ambience and more.

14
00:00:53.543 --> 00:00:55.999
Hang one charm, or two side by side.

15
00:00:56.049 --> 00:01:00.106
Toro and Kuro have living cat faces — click
one to poke it.

16
00:01:00.156 --> 00:01:04.700
And themes set both charms, a soft glow, and a
sound in one click.

17
00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:09.249
Every so often, a desk visitor drops by.

18
00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:12.639
A baby elephant trumpets and sprays the charm.

19
00:01:12.689 --> 00:01:14.925
A cat stretches and settles in.

20
00:01:14.975 --> 00:01:17.136
A cheeky monkey steals a bead!

21
00:01:17.186 --> 00:01:19.200
And a peacock fans its tail.

22
00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:23.536
The yogi floats in for three slow breaths.

23
00:01:23.586 --> 00:01:26.077
The chai-wala rides up with your break.

24
00:01:26.127 --> 00:01:29.725
And the myna bird lands to remind you to rest
your eyes.

25
00:01:31.375 --> 00:01:35.400
Vijay, your water buddy, offers a tumbler:
drink some water?

26
00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:38.863
Say yes, and a glass is counted on your water
ring.

27
00:01:38.913 --> 00:01:44.500
During festivals like Pongal, Holi, Diwali and
Christmas, special guests visit too.

28
00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:49.761
When you need a pause, start a guided
breathing session.

29
00:01:49.811 --> 00:01:53.094
The charm glows — in for four seconds, out for
six.

30
00:01:53.144 --> 00:01:54.075
Just follow it.

31
00:01:55.725 --> 00:02:00.503
The focus timer gives you twenty-five minutes
of focus, then a short break.

32
00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:05.975
It asks what you are working on, and shows
your task and time right beside the charm.

33
00:02:07.625 --> 00:02:09.984
The water ring fills through the day.

34
00:02:10.034 --> 00:02:12.002
The yogi leads a quick stretch.

35
00:02:12.052 --> 00:02:17.275
And once a day, a mood check-in asks how you
are feeling, with five simple faces.

36
00:02:18.925 --> 00:02:26.481
Your own reminders arrive as a soft cue beside
the charm, a visitor if you like, and a
Windows notification.

37
00:02:26.531 --> 00:02:33.875
Add gentle ambience — rain, ocean, temple, or
chimes — and a daily ritual for your mornings
and evenings.

38
00:02:35.525 --> 00:02:40.891
Insights shows your calm minutes, breaks,
water and streak, with a look at this week.

39
00:02:40.941 --> 00:02:47.200
And Settings lets you shape everything: the
charm, play, visitors, calm tools, seasons and
privacy.

40
00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:52.059
The charm and visitors can speak English or
Tamil.

41
00:02:52.109 --> 00:02:59.750
Set shortcuts to send a visitor, count a glass
of water, or take a breath, and back up your
settings to a single file.

42
00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.751
Best of all, it stays on your PC.

43
00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:06.515
No account, no analytics, no tracking.

44
00:03:06.565 --> 00:03:10.225
DeskCharm — a little calm, hanging on your
desktop.
